(6970396, 1051112, 30982, '<td valign="top">I normally don''t go for selective desat, but I can see this as an ad for a clothing line.  The kid has an adorable expression and amazing eyes, too.</td>', 'I normally don''t go for selective desat, but I can see this as an ad for a clothing line.  The kid has an adorable expression and amazing eyes, too.', '2013-02-03 01:01:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6970402, 1051188, 97166, '<td valign="top">When their windswept bones were found, some years later, facing apart with som distance between them, the rest of the herd could never figure out how these two, who had been so much in love, could end up in such a way.<br/> <br/>The answer, had it ever been discovered, was simpler than they could ever imagine. Indeed, these two were a tragedy, and it never needed to happen. All Arnold ever needed to do was stop to ask directions.</td>', 'When their windswept bones were found, some years later, facing apart with som distance between them, the rest of the herd could never figure out how these two, who had been so much in love, could end up in such a way. The answer, had it ever been discovered, was simpler than they could ever imagine. Indeed, these two were a tragedy, and it never needed to happen. All Arnold ever needed to do was stop to ask directions.', '2013-02-03 01:48:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(6970403, 1052045, 97166, '<td valign="top">It was in the dark, at the end of the day, when it was hardest. When the weight of the world settled in on him. When he felt he had no-one to talk to, nowhere to turn. When the trials of school, and the other kids, who were always so cruel, became so much to bear. <br/> <br/>But he wouldn''t give in to the pain. He wouldn''t give in to the tears. And while his eyes betrayed a sadness and anger within, he would remain stoic. He would fight through. He would have strength no matter how much the darkness closed in.<br/> <br/>He would FIND the light, and he would persevere.</td>', 'It was in the dark, at the end of the day, when it was hardest. When the weight of the world settled in on him. When he felt he had no-one to talk to, nowhere to turn. When the trials of school, and the other kids, who were always so cruel, became so much to bear.  But he wouldn''t give in to the pain. He wouldn''t give in to the tears. And while his eyes betrayed a sadness and anger within, he would remain stoic. He would fight through. He would have strength no matter how much the darkness closed in. He would FIND the light, and he would persevere.', '2013-02-03 01:53:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6970404, 1051906, 97166, '<td valign="top">At the end, all he had was the memories.<br/> <br/>The young couple so much in love, that had purchased him for their newlywed home. Their passion and happiness, in the beginning, had filled him with pride and joy. <br/> <br/>The children that came later, to climb over him and play games like hide and seek, giggling as they hid behind.<br/> <br/>The stories told to toddlers in laps.<br/> <br/>The caresses given in love and companionship.<br/> <br/>The quiet afternoons in font of the fire, with one or another relaxing upon him with a good book.<br/> <br/>The comfort given as she sat and cried, curled up, lamenting the loss of her beloved.<br/> <br/>The endless nights knitting for the grandchildren.<br/> <br/>The glorious return of childhood when those grandchildren would visit.<br/> <br/>The final days, when she became sick and spent so much time within his cushion.<br/> <br/>In the end, all he had were the memories, and they were all he needed.</td>', 'At the end, all he had was the memories. The young couple so much in love, that had purchased him for their newlywed home. Their passion and happiness, in the beginning, had filled him with pride and joy.  The children that came later, to climb over him and play games like hide and seek, giggling as they hid behind. The stories told to toddlers in laps. The caresses given in love and companionship. The quiet afternoons in font of the fire, with one or another relaxing upon him with a good book. The comfort given as she sat and cried, curled up, lamenting the loss of her beloved. The endless nights knitting for the grandchildren. The glorious return of childhood when those grandchildren would visit. The final days, when she became sick and spent so much time within his cushion. In the end, all he had were the memories, and they were all he needed.', '2013-02-03 02:02:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6970405, 1052059, 97166, '<td valign="top">"... And then, you won''t believe it, after he saved the nest, after he saved it, he, I''m serious, he FLEW away. He flew! Like a super-hero! I''M SERIOUS."<br/> <br/>They all just looked at him, and blinked a few times, but nobody ever had the heart to tell him. They had to hear a new story like this every day, but they could never bring themselves to tell him.</td>', '"... And then, you won''t believe it, after he saved the nest, after he saved it, he, I''m serious, he FLEW away. He flew! Like a super-hero! I''M SERIOUS." They all just looked at him, and blinked a few times, but nobody ever had the heart to tell him. They had to hear a new story like this every day, but they could never bring themselves to tell him.', '2013-02-03 02:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6970406, 1052104, 97166, '<td valign="top">Charise just rolled her eyes and shook her head. Every time. EVERY time. As soon as the photographer showed up, Arnold would inevitably try to show off with "Jazz Hands". <br/> <br/>She sighed, what was worse is that he thought everyone was laughing WITH him.</td>', 'Charise just rolled her eyes and shook her head. Every time. EVERY time. As soon as the photographer showed up, Arnold would inevitably try to show off with "Jazz Hands".  She sighed, what was worse is that he thought everyone was laughing WITH him.', '2013-02-03 02:16:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6970407, 1049998, 97166, '<td valign="top">Although one might think it would be an incredible talent, Jim''s ability to fish in Super-speed never really amounted to much.  Indeed, he was the laughing stock of the Superhero community.<br/> <br/>Then again, at least he wasn''t George, he of the ability to project an orange dot on the wall.</td>', 'Although one might think it would be an incredible talent, Jim''s ability to fish in Super-speed never really amounted to much.  Indeed, he was the laughing stock of the Superhero community. Then again, at least he wasn''t George, he of the ability to project an orange dot on the wall.', '2013-02-03 02:20:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6970413, 1051114, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style!<br/> <br/>(Voted earlier)<br/> <br/>This is one of my 10s - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:<br/> <br/>1. The coloration: I love that cross-processed look, offering a slightly vintage feel.<br/> <br/>2. Fantastic clarity of your subject - you''ve nailed the focus and used a narrow depth of field to isolate your subject; you''ve anchored the eye wonderfully but we are all too aware of the context.<br/> <br/>3. A great sense of story - why is she off on her own like that? What is she leaving behind? Is there a car hiding over the hill?<br/> <br/>4. Your POV - your low angle does great things to the perspective of the image and adds a considered cinematic appeal.<br/> <br/>Overall: Beautifully balanced shot, well conceived and superbly executed.</td>', 'This is a new comment series for me, so please bear with me while I find my style! (Voted earlier) This is one of my 10s - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: 1. The coloration: I love that cross-processed look, offering a slightly vintage feel. 2. Fantastic clarity of your subject - you''ve nailed the focus and used a narrow depth of field to isolate your subject; you''ve anchored the eye wonderfully but we are all too aware of the context. 3. A great sense of story - why is she off on her own like that? What is she leaving behind? Is there a car hiding over the hill? 4. Your POV - your low angle does great things to the perspective of the image and adds a considered cinematic appeal. Overall: Beautifully balanced shot, well conceived and superbly executed.', '2013-02-03 02:36:15.000000', NULL, 1),
