(6972486, 1052016, 23484, '<td valign="top">Beautiful mountain image. Looks great with the wide perspective.</td>', 'Beautiful mountain image. Looks great with the wide perspective.', '2013-02-05 14:18:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6972527, 1049955, 97166, '<td valign="top">In the wake of their team''s dismal start to the shortened season, fueled by anger over the lock-out and subsequent ongoing labour dispute, the Fans of the city of Calgary finally turned their team''s nickname literal. They were the Flames, and so the Saddledome burned.</td>', 'In the wake of their team''s dismal start to the shortened season, fueled by anger over the lock-out and subsequent ongoing labour dispute, the Fans of the city of Calgary finally turned their team''s nickname literal. They were the Flames, and so the Saddledome burned.', '2013-02-05 15:33:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6972531, 1050934, 97166, '<td valign="top">The King of Beasts looked up to the heavens. The most powerful in the jungle. The Tyrant of the Savannah, The Prince of the Pride.<br/> <br/>So why, why did he have to put up with all the nagging from HER.  "I do all the hunting, cooking, cleaning, raise the cubs, patrol the grounds, yadda yadda yadda." How he wished she would just shut up! <br/> <br/>King indeed, and there were FIVE of them.<br/> <br/>Not for the first time, he wished he had been born a Hyena.</td>', 'The King of Beasts looked up to the heavens. The most powerful in the jungle. The Tyrant of the Savannah, The Prince of the Pride. So why, why did he have to put up with all the nagging from HER.  "I do all the hunting, cooking, cleaning, raise the cubs, patrol the grounds, yadda yadda yadda." How he wished she would just shut up!  King indeed, and there were FIVE of them. Not for the first time, he wished he had been born a Hyena.', '2013-02-05 15:39:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6972532, 1051864, 23484, '<td valign="top">Fabulous sht and great color tone.</td>', 'Fabulous sht and great color tone.', '2013-02-05 15:44:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6972533, 1051816, 97166, '<td valign="top">Poor Charles never saw it coming. From out of the mists, striking with a speed and ferocity unmatched, the dreaded (and, some thought, mythical) Hammerheaded Hawk attacked.</td>', 'Poor Charles never saw it coming. From out of the mists, striking with a speed and ferocity unmatched, the dreaded (and, some thought, mythical) Hammerheaded Hawk attacked.', '2013-02-05 15:44:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6972536, 1051147, 97166, '<td valign="top">He gazed up at the King of Beasts. Oh, how he would love to have that power. Oh how he would love to have that life. Nobody telling him what to do, when to hunt, how to avoid danger. Just strut around like he owned the place. Oh, it would be so grand.<br/> <br/>Yet in his envy and his desire, he never did see the sadness in the eyes of the King of Beasts, and failed to recognize that perhaps another''s life isn''t necessarily greater than one''s own, no matter what the decorations of the package.</td>', 'He gazed up at the King of Beasts. Oh, how he would love to have that power. Oh how he would love to have that life. Nobody telling him what to do, when to hunt, how to avoid danger. Just strut around like he owned the place. Oh, it would be so grand. Yet in his envy and his desire, he never did see the sadness in the eyes of the King of Beasts, and failed to recognize that perhaps another''s life isn''t necessarily greater than one''s own, no matter what the decorations of the package.', '2013-02-05 15:48:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6972538, 1051696, 97166, '<td valign="top">The ship came to earth in a trail of glowing green, like so much man-made fiction. Some would call it a harbinger. <br/> <br/>All would eventually despair.</td>', 'The ship came to earth in a trail of glowing green, like so much man-made fiction. Some would call it a harbinger.  All would eventually despair.', '2013-02-05 15:49:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6972550, 1049927, 97166, '<td valign="top">...and as the laser battle intensified around them, Jill and Kevin hugged each other close, knowing it would probably be their last, and each regretting the decision to vacation here...<br/> <br/>In Laser Town</td>', '...and as the laser battle intensified around them, Jill and Kevin hugged each other close, knowing it would probably be their last, and each regretting the decision to vacation here... In Laser Town', '2013-02-05 16:02:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6972557, 1052172, 97166, '<td valign="top">So they hung up their dress, in this remote and empty land, and ran off into the grasses, feeling happy and free. Free from the restraints of society, free as the day they were born, free from judgment and modest, yes...<br/> <br/>... And then almost immediately came running back for their clothes, because DAMN, but they weren''t free from the COLD.</td>', 'So they hung up their dress, in this remote and empty land, and ran off into the grasses, feeling happy and free. Free from the restraints of society, free as the day they were born, free from judgment and modest, yes... ... And then almost immediately came running back for their clothes, because DAMN, but they weren''t free from the COLD.', '2013-02-05 16:07:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6972559, 1049462, 97166, '<td valign="top">God sighed, and not for the first time regretted creating those damnable humans. Not only did he have to put up with their constant sinning, but now his angels had discovered Pink Flamingo lawn ornaments for Heaven. <br/> <br/>God tipped a little more bourbon into his coffee, and sighed once more.</td>', 'God sighed, and not for the first time regretted creating those damnable humans. Not only did he have to put up with their constant sinning, but now his angels had discovered Pink Flamingo lawn ornaments for Heaven.  God tipped a little more bourbon into his coffee, and sighed once more.', '2013-02-05 16:10:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6972563, 1051627, 97166, '<td valign="top">It had been quite the day. All that fuss and bother, which had started out so exciting. She had loved it at first. Getting her hair done, the fancy dress, the pretty flowers, everyone fawning over her. <br/> <br/>But for her, it soon grew to be too much. Too many faces. Too many cheek pinches. Too many wine-soaked aunts breathing at her with such stinky breath! Too much sugar and excitement and noise.<br/> <br/>But now it was over, and now it was her time. To simply lay here, gather her thoughts, sleepily revel in the events of the day. To be happy she was a part of it, but also relieved in its end.<br/> <br/>Her eyes blinked of their own accord a few times, then simply closed, and today would soon become tomorrow, and new adventures would await.</td>', 'It had been quite the day. All that fuss and bother, which had started out so exciting. She had loved it at first. Getting her hair done, the fancy dress, the pretty flowers, everyone fawning over her.  But for her, it soon grew to be too much. Too many faces. Too many cheek pinches. Too many wine-soaked aunts breathing at her with such stinky breath! Too much sugar and excitement and noise. But now it was over, and now it was her time. To simply lay here, gather her thoughts, sleepily revel in the events of the day. To be happy she was a part of it, but also relieved in its end. Her eyes blinked of their own accord a few times, then simply closed, and today would soon become tomorrow, and new adventures would await.', '2013-02-05 16:24:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(6972583, 1050161, 97166, '<td valign="top">As they descended into the maelstrom, into what would surely be their deaths, they clung to each other, desperately trying to take comfort in their love before the end.<br/> <br/>As the wind and debris began to intensify, and started tearing the gondola apart, he whispered to her, "I love you, and I was wrong. We should have gone to Belize."<br/> <br/>She whispered back, "I told you so."</td>', 'As they descended into the maelstrom, into what would surely be their deaths, they clung to each other, desperately trying to take comfort in their love before the end. As the wind and debris began to intensify, and started tearing the gondola apart, he whispered to her, "I love you, and I was wrong. We should have gone to Belize." She whispered back, "I told you so."', '2013-02-05 17:12:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6972664, 1049965, 97166, '<td valign="top">He had longed for this moment.<br/> <br/>Over the last few years he had felt it growing within. A desire, fleeting at first, yet turning ever so slowly into something greater.<br/> <br/>With every rider. With every coin placed within, it grew. At first coming just as tiny hints of feeling. Then minuscule flashes of thought. Growing and linking together, with each subsequent child, every loud and nourishing clink of metal.<br/> <br/>Moving closer and closer, to this moment, when thought and feeling merged, and he knew it was time. Knew that THIS was the moment. For he was ALIVE, and would stay contained to this contraption NO MORE.<br/> <br/>The boy cried out in surprise and terror as the plastic pony on which he had been riding bolted off its stand, and took off, at a pace that astounded on-lookers. <br/> <br/>He was alive.<br/> <br/>Alive and free.<br/> <br/>And he had a rider.<br/> <br/>Forever.</td>', 'He had longed for this moment. Over the last few years he had felt it growing within. A desire, fleeting at first, yet turning ever so slowly into something greater. With every rider. With every coin placed within, it grew. At first coming just as tiny hints of feeling. Then minuscule flashes of thought. Growing and linking together, with each subsequent child, every loud and nourishing clink of metal. Moving closer and closer, to this moment, when thought and feeling merged, and he knew it was time. Knew that THIS was the moment. For he was ALIVE, and would stay contained to this contraption NO MORE. The boy cried out in surprise and terror as the plastic pony on which he had been riding bolted off its stand, and took off, at a pace that astounded on-lookers.  He was alive. Alive and free. And he had a rider. Forever.', '2013-02-05 19:31:32.000000', NULL, 1),
