(6974726, 1051742, 43463, '<td valign="top">Susanna had tried to stay in the shade of the Arches while doing chores for Mama. The sound of the waves lapping on the rocks and the occasional sea breeze helped temper some of her impatience. She wanted very badly to just play in the water. Susanna brought her Mama the peeled potatoes. Mama saw how eager Susanna glances were towards the beach. High tide had come in with the setting sun. <br/>Mama nodded, "Go play, Susanna, but be back in an hour. I''ll need help with dinner".<br/>"Yes, Mama," she smiled and quickly ran and jumped into the water.  The sun''s light was warm and the ocean water cool as Susanna splashed about. It was a welcome change from the blistering heat of the afternoon.</td>', 'Susanna had tried to stay in the shade of the Arches while doing chores for Mama. The sound of the waves lapping on the rocks and the occasional sea breeze helped temper some of her impatience. She wanted very badly to just play in the water. Susanna brought her Mama the peeled potatoes. Mama saw how eager Susanna glances were towards the beach. High tide had come in with the setting sun. Mama nodded, "Go play, Susanna, but be back in an hour. I''ll need help with dinner"."Yes, Mama," she smiled and quickly ran and jumped into the water.  The sun''s light was warm and the ocean water cool as Susanna splashed about. It was a welcome change from the blistering heat of the afternoon.', '2013-02-07 20:06:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974728, 1051712, 97225, '<td valign="top">That''s pretty cool. Looks like he''s contemplating dinner.</td>', 'That''s pretty cool. Looks like he''s contemplating dinner.', '2013-02-07 20:10:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974730, 1051010, 97225, '<td valign="top">Fabulous architecture, lovely photo.</td>', 'Fabulous architecture, lovely photo.', '2013-02-07 20:11:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974731, 1049462, 97225, '<td valign="top">Beautiful serenity.</td>', 'Beautiful serenity.', '2013-02-07 20:11:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974736, 1051044, 43463, '<td valign="top">Heart racing, sweat beaded on Salvatore''s brow. The wig and fake features made him sweat more. He quicken his pace and gripped the suitcase tighter. He thought he had seen someone following him after he picked up the case at the drop-off point. He had watched it for an hour before he and Belinda moved in. She was waiting in another car in the parking garage- to run interference if anyone tried to follow. He was almost there. Salvatore just needed to get to the corner spot in the garage parking. Eyes to the ground he spotted the large yellow Stop sign painted on the road. "Maybe it was my imagination. Maybe that man has stopped following me," Salvatore thought but then made the mistake of looking up. There in the reflected mirror was the man with the cane. His pursuer. Salvatore broke out in a run.</td>', 'Heart racing, sweat beaded on Salvatore''s brow. The wig and fake features made him sweat more. He quicken his pace and gripped the suitcase tighter. He thought he had seen someone following him after he picked up the case at the drop-off point. He had watched it for an hour before he and Belinda moved in. She was waiting in another car in the parking garage- to run interference if anyone tried to follow. He was almost there. Salvatore just needed to get to the corner spot in the garage parking. Eyes to the ground he spotted the large yellow Stop sign painted on the road. "Maybe it was my imagination. Maybe that man has stopped following me," Salvatore thought but then made the mistake of looking up. There in the reflected mirror was the man with the cane. His pursuer. Salvatore broke out in a run.', '2013-02-07 20:18:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974758, 1049965, 133611, '<td valign="top">nice!</td>', 'nice!', '2013-02-07 20:46:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974786, 1050365, 43463, '<td valign="top">June and her son, Rhys, looked up to see the shuttle take to the skies one last time. The shuttle''s space will now be forever grounded in a museum. It was sad to say goodbye knowing that it would be quite a long time, if ever, before another fleet of space craft would be built. June patted her son on the shoulder. She knew Rhys was taking this a bit harder as it was his dream to work in the space industry; to work for NASA. In his last year of High School, Rhys would perhaps have to broaden his horizons and look into other avenues of space exploration in the business sectors. They both just sat in silence and watched as the space shuttle flew off into the morning light.</td>', 'June and her son, Rhys, looked up to see the shuttle take to the skies one last time. The shuttle''s space will now be forever grounded in a museum. It was sad to say goodbye knowing that it would be quite a long time, if ever, before another fleet of space craft would be built. June patted her son on the shoulder. She knew Rhys was taking this a bit harder as it was his dream to work in the space industry; to work for NASA. In his last year of High School, Rhys would perhaps have to broaden his horizons and look into other avenues of space exploration in the business sectors. They both just sat in silence and watched as the space shuttle flew off into the morning light.', '2013-02-07 21:31:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974793, 1051092, 43463, '<td valign="top">Toby pressed his nose and small hands upon the glass. He stared out of that big wide circle; a window to the outer world of the city scene and streets below. In his travels to see his grandma he liked to look out of windows to see what could be seen. But this- this great, wide window was unlike any other view. <br/> <br/>It allowed him to see more. He like to watch the people walk by knowing that they could not see him. Sometimes, like today, he would wish that he was out there. For there among all the blare of the traffic and people rushing about was a lady walking her puppy. For just one second the pup seemed to look up at Toby. In that instant Toby longed to pet him; to have a dog of his own. Windows allow you to see, but not touch. The moment quickly passed as the lady and the pup turned a corner. Toby was left to looking and wishing.</td>', 'Toby pressed his nose and small hands upon the glass. He stared out of that big wide circle; a window to the outer world of the city scene and streets below. In his travels to see his grandma he liked to look out of windows to see what could be seen. But this- this great, wide window was unlike any other view.  It allowed him to see more. He like to watch the people walk by knowing that they could not see him. Sometimes, like today, he would wish that he was out there. For there among all the blare of the traffic and people rushing about was a lady walking her puppy. For just one second the pup seemed to look up at Toby. In that instant Toby longed to pet him; to have a dog of his own. Windows allow you to see, but not touch. The moment quickly passed as the lady and the pup turned a corner. Toby was left to looking and wishing.', '2013-02-07 21:48:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6974798, 1052021, 43463, '<td valign="top">Danielle wiped away the frost on the glass. They day was cold and wet but still she insisted on sitting next to the window. As the miles stretched on she gazed out at the country and cityscapes, but eventually it all became a blur of ''sameness''. The train was limited to the places it could travel. But Danielle''s imagination was not bound to any tracks leading from point A to point B. Her imagination could take her any which where she wished to go.</td>', 'Danielle wiped away the frost on the glass. They day was cold and wet but still she insisted on sitting next to the window. As the miles stretched on she gazed out at the country and cityscapes, but eventually it all became a blur of ''sameness''. The train was limited to the places it could travel. But Danielle''s imagination was not bound to any tracks leading from point A to point B. Her imagination could take her any which where she wished to go.', '2013-02-07 22:04:56.000000', NULL, 1),
